# Build the guided calibration session

## Scope and existing evidence

Historical implementation notes are retained for provenance. The accepted
finite design does not imply unfinished runtime integration exists.

Collect isolated characters, joins, words, numerals, punctuation, mathematics,
titles, labels, sizes, speeds, pressure proxies, and free writing on known
paper.

Current executable evidence now freezes transport-neutral calibration
provenance. Parameter evidence retains caller-owned source region, units,
confidence, and accepted correction history; observed evidence remains distinct
from inferred extremes. Training and held-out sample identities cannot cross
roles, and an underdetermined required behavior explicitly requests another
sample.

A 5,461-case exhaustive compact oracle covers every declaration sequence through
six samples over two identities and both roles. Repeated same-role declarations
remain valid while the first cross-role reuse rejects in declaration order.
Successful separation now returns constructor-sealed evidence borrowing the
exact sample declaration slice, and the same oracle requires direct/sealed
parity.

This does not choose a minimum sample set, confidence scale, unit vocabulary,
source-region syntax, capture geometry, extraction algorithm, or calibration
workflow.

Guided-session evidence now also preserves a caller-supplied ordered prompt plan
across resumptions, rejects duplicate prompt identities, derives completion from
accepted prompt progress, and covers the ADR's isolated-character, join, word,
sentence, numeral, punctuation, mathematical-symbol, heading, and free-writing
categories. Successful identity admission now seals the exact session so
completed prompts, completion, and next-pending position can be projected
without rescanning identities.

An exhaustive 511-state compact corpus covers every pending/completed mask from
zero through eight prompts and cross-checks direct and sealed completion,
next-pending position, and completed-prompt inspection against an independent
bit-mask oracle. One
exact-precondition edit can replace a completed prompt's sample link while
preserving all unrelated prompt state; stale, pending, missing, ambiguous, and
no-op cases cannot alter the session. A second exhaustive 3,076-case compact
oracle crosses prompt counts through six with every progress mask, target or
missing target, current/stale expectation, and equal/different replacement.

Minimum counts, wording, sufficiency, weak-sample classification and workflow
policy, capture UI, persistence/history, and geometry semantics remain open.

## Finite guided A4 calibration worksheet and completion contract

**Inputs:** a selected A4 physical worksheet revision, one declared profile
identity, a fixed ordered prompt plan, and caller-recorded sample evidence.
**Outputs:** a printed worksheet specification and a resumable completion
ledger that marks each prompt `Pending`, `Completed` or `NeedsRecapture`.
An incomplete or low-confidence worksheet cannot establish a usable writer.

**Worksheet:** print an A4 portrait page with four 10 mm fiducial crosses at
`(15,15)`, `(195,15)`, `(195,282)`, `(15,282)` mm in page coordinates, a
printed identity/revision label, and isolated ruled capture boxes. Leave
sufficient room for pen entry/exit and baseline marks. Prompt identifiers
must be stable across resumption and a retake must preserve prior provenance,
not overwrite a sample silently.

| Prompt ID | Role and requested sample | Evidence captured |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `c01` | Body `a m n o` isolated | Stroke starts, ends and lifts |
| `c02` | Join `an mano` | Adjacent-letter joining |
| `c03` | Word `mañana` | Word spacing and diacritic |
| `c04` | Sentence `¿Dónde estás?` | Punctuation and line rhythm |
| `c05` | Numerals `0123456789` | Numeric joins and scale |
| `c06` | Symbols `¡ ? « » —` | Prose punctuation |
| `c07` | Mathematics `x² + 1 = 2` | Symbol role and baseline |
| `c08` | Title `Biología` | Title height and scale |
| `c09` | Label `Figura A` | Compact label size |
| `c10` | Free writing, two lines | Unprompted rhythm and speed |

**Collection rule:** each accepted prompt names the exact sample region,
source capture identity, physical unit, pen/writer declaration and observed
provenance. Speed and pressure proxies are only caller-reported or measured
with a declared method; static photos cannot invent pressure values. Reserve
separately labeled held-out sample IDs for later comparison and prohibit
reusing any training ID as held-out evidence. Confidence must state whether
observed, inferred, or unknown rather than fabricate a numeric score.

**Worked example:** `student-A` has `c01` through `c07` completed, with `c08`
marked `NeedsRecapture` and `c09`/`c10` pending. The resumable ledger reports
`7/10` accepted, next actionable prompt `c08`, and overall `Incomplete`.
Replacing `c08` requires its exact current sample reference and a fresh
capture ID; the other nine records and original sample provenance remain.

**Refusal example:** duplicate `c04`, a sample reused as both training and
held-out, a stale replacement identity, absent fiducials or a missing capture
rejects the relevant admission with a visible reason. Completion cannot be
inferred from merely touching all ten prompts if capture quality is unknown.
A photograph of the sheet is not proof of measured stroke geometry.

**Assumptions and limits:** ordered prompt identity, progress/retake checks,
sample provenance and training/held-out separation exist as transport-neutral
primitives. Worksheet generation, camera capture, paper calibration,
confidence scoring and live UI do not. These ten prompts are a finite
**design worksheet**, not collected evidence or an authenticated user profile.

## Acceptance decision

- **Basis:** practical for prompt-progress and provenance primitives;
  theoretical for the A4 worksheet and capture UX, 2026-11-02.
- **Delivered:** ten finite prompts covering all named roles, four fiducials,
  completion states, one incomplete example and explicit refusal paths.
- **Not implemented by this acceptance:** physical worksheet printing,
  real camera workflow, capture-quality scoring or extracted strokes.
